  "D1_explicit_sqrt_convention": "Balanced A4.SS1 states bounded Borel spectral calculus and that a nonnegative operator has a unique nonnegative square root. Thus Gamma_P positive root convention is explicitly given by D.1, not merely inferred. Its concrete Lean construction remains unproved here.",
  "D2_marginal_curvature": "D.6 invokes Bakry-Emery Poincare for strong logconcavity; D.10 uses Hess U_eta=eta^-1(I-Sigma_y) and conditional covariance bounds. Equation2.13 gives alpha/(1+alpha eta)<=Hess U_eta<=beta/(1+beta eta). C.3 consumes Poincare constant1/alpha+eta on actual nu.",
  "weighted_laplacian_omission": "No source weighted-Laplacian, gradient-adjoint operator/domain or resolvent Gamma definition. Inferred grad_nu*=-div+gradW dot, nonnegative grad_nu*grad versus nonpositive diffusion generator remains authored background. No eta-scaled resolvent coefficient can be extracted.",
  "Gamma_inverse_scope": "Gamma inverse bounded on H_P,0 only after B.15. A inverse only on positive [1/2,1] spectral band in C.28. All-L2 Gamma norm identity is distinct from either inverse.",
  "coefficient_precision": "Gamma sqrt/norm identity no eta coefficient. B.13 left4eta; C.2 lefteta with c=(1-alpha eta)^2/[4(1+alpha eta)]. Marginal Poincare constant1/alpha+eta. C.28 uses sqrteta.",
